IMPORT prelude

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore) -- ss 8, 9 and 13 to 19.
--
-- The rest of the Act, after the eligibility and recovery rules in sss-act.l4.
-- Two very different things sit here: the INFORMATION regime in ss 8 and 9,
-- which is the machinery that makes an automatic means-tested scheme possible,
-- and the ordinary administrative provisions in ss 13 to 19.
--
-- ss 8 and 9 deserve the attention. The Scheme pays people without their
-- applying, which means the Government must assemble means information about
-- them from other departments. s 8 compels that disclosure and s 9 limits what
-- may then be done with it. Those two sections are where the privacy of every
-- recipient is decided.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 1 to 5 (purpose, administration, the Board's functions),
-- s 18 (conduct of prosecutions) and s 20 (regulations).

§ `Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 -- sections 8, 9 and 13 to 19`

§§ `8 -- Compelled disclosure between departments`

-- s 8(1): where the MINISTER CERTIFIES IN WRITING that it is necessary for an
-- authorised person to have access to a particular class of MEANS INFORMATION
-- held by a Government department or public authority, in order to facilitate
-- the administration or enforcement of the Act or the administration of the
-- Scheme, then the Minister responsible for that department "MAY ... DIRECT"
-- it to provide "SO MUCH OF the means information AS IS NECESSARY for that
-- purpose"; and that department "IS TO COMPLY ..., DESPITE ANY OTHER WRITTEN
-- LAW, AND WHETHER OR NOT IT IS UNDER ANY OBLIGATION ... NOT TO DISCLOSE such
-- information."
--
-- s 8(2) is the same machinery for CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION other than means
-- information, to an "information recipient" rather than an authorised person.
--
-- Three safeguards are built in, and all three are conditions rather than
-- discretions: a written certificate of necessity, a limit to what is
-- necessary, and a stated purpose. The duty to comply is absolute once they
-- are met.
DECLARE InformationKind IS ONE OF
    `means information`                                 -- s 8(1)
    `confidential information other than means information` -- s 8(2)

DECLARE DisclosureDirection HAS
    `the kind`                                  IS AN InformationKind
    `the Minister certified in writing that access is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose is the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the responsible Minister directed the department or public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no more than is necessary for that purpose was directed to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recipient is an authorised person`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recipient is an information recipient` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The recipient differs between the two subsections: (1) goes to an authorised
-- person, (2) to an information recipient.
GIVEN `the direction` IS A DisclosureDirection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient matches the subsection` IF
    CONSIDER `the direction`'s `the kind`
    WHEN `means information` THEN `the direction`'s `the recipient is an authorised person`
    OTHERWISE `the direction`'s `the recipient is an information recipient`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A DisclosureDirection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction is validly given` IF
        `the direction`'s `the Minister certified in writing that access is necessary`
    AND `the direction`'s `the purpose is the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme`
    AND `the direction`'s `the responsible Minister directed the department or public authority`
    AND `the direction`'s `no more than is necessary for that purpose was directed to be provided`
    AND `the recipient matches the subsection` `the direction`

-- The department must comply "DESPITE ANY OTHER WRITTEN LAW, AND WHETHER OR
-- NOT IT IS UNDER ANY OBLIGATION ... NOT TO DISCLOSE". So an existing duty of
-- confidence is no answer -- but only where the direction was validly given.
GIVEN `the direction` IS A DisclosureDirection
    , `the department is under an obligation not to disclose the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the department must comply with the direction` IF
    `the direction is validly given` `the direction`

§§ `9 -- What may then be done with the information`

-- s 9(2): use or disclosure of information obtained under s 8, WITHOUT THE
-- CONSENT of the individual, "is AUTHORISED ONLY IF the purpose ... is to
-- communicate or manage the information as part of -- (a) the administration or
-- enforcement of this Act; or (b) the administration of the Scheme."
--
-- A closed purpose test. Anything else needs consent.
DECLARE UsePurpose IS ONE OF
    `the administration or enforcement of this Act`     -- (a)
    `the administration of the Scheme`                  -- (b)
    `some other purpose`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A UsePurpose, `the individual consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use or disclosure is authorised by section 9(2)` IF
        `the individual consented`
    OR  `the purpose is one section 9(2) names` `the purpose`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A UsePurpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is one section 9(2) names` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `some other purpose` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 9(3): DESPITE s 9(2), information DERIVED FROM what was obtained under s 8
-- may go to a public officer, public authority or any other person or
-- organisation, for the development or implementation of a PRESCRIBED public
-- scheme --
--   (a) only at their request AND with the Minister's approval; and
--   (b) only in the form of a REPORT stating (i) whether the individual
--       satisfies the eligibility criteria for a benefit, and (ii) the
--       description and amount of each benefit they are eligible for or have
--       received up to the date of the report.
--
-- So the carve-out is tightly shaped: derived information only, a prescribed
-- scheme only, on request, with approval, and only in that two-item form.
DECLARE OnwardReport HAS
    `the information is derived from information obtained under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the receiving scheme is prescribed for the purposes of section 9(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was requested by the recipient`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister approved`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is in the form of a report stating only the two matters in section 9(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual has opted out and the Commissioner, Board or administrator has been notified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual consented despite having opted out` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the report` IS AN OnwardReport
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 9(3) conditions are met` IF
        `the report`'s `the information is derived from information obtained under section 8`
    AND `the report`'s `the receiving scheme is prescribed for the purposes of section 9(3)`
    AND `the report`'s `it was requested by the recipient`
    AND `the report`'s `the Minister approved`
    AND `the report`'s `it is in the form of a report stating only the two matters in section 9(3)(b)`

-- s 9(5): if an individual OPTS OUT, "in the manner determined by the
-- Commissioner", then from the time of notification the report "MUST NOT" be
-- provided about them, "EXCEPT WITH THE CONSENT of the individual."
--
-- An opt-out, not an opt-in: the reports flow unless the person stops them, and
-- the burden is on the individual to find out that they can.
GIVEN `the report` IS AN OnwardReport
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(5) forbids providing the report` IF
        `the report`'s `the individual has opted out and the Commissioner, Board or administrator has been notified`
    AND NOT `the report`'s `the individual consented despite having opted out`

GIVEN `the report` IS AN OnwardReport
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report may lawfully be provided` IF
        `the section 9(3) conditions are met` `the report`
    AND NOT `section 9(5) forbids providing the report` `the report`

-- s 9(7): contravening s 9(2), (3) or (5) is an offence -- a fine not exceeding
-- $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both. Note that the same
-- maximum attaches to misusing a recipient's private information as attaches,
-- under s 11, to obtaining a grant by a dishonest lie.
`the maximum fine under section 9(7) in dollars` MEANS 5000
`the maximum imprisonment under section 9(7) in months` MEANS 12

§§ `13 -- The administrator's certificate`

-- s 13: a certificate purporting to be issued by an administrator certifying
-- (a) the amount received, or (b) the amount recoverable, "is PRIMA FACIE
-- EVIDENCE that the amount so stated was received by that person or is
-- recoverable from that person ... as at that date."
--
-- Prima facie, so rebuttable -- but the burden has moved. The recipient must
-- displace the administrator's own figure.
DECLARE Certificate IS ONE OF
    `the amount of benefit received as at a date`       -- (a)
    `the amount recoverable as at a date`               -- (b)
    `something else`

GIVEN `the certificate` IS A Certificate
    , `it purports to be issued by an administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is prima facie evidence of the amount` IF
        `it purports to be issued by an administrator`
    AND `the certificate is of a kind section 13 names` `the certificate`

GIVEN `the certificate` IS A Certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is of a kind section 13 names` IF
    CONSIDER `the certificate`
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `14 and 15 -- The powers to obtain information, and obstruction`

-- s 14(4): a person required to provide information or produce a document who
-- "REFUSES OR FAILS, WITHOUT REASONABLE EXCUSE, to do so WITHIN THE TIME
-- ALLOWED" commits an offence -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment
-- not exceeding 6 months or both.
DECLARE InformationRequirement HAS
    `the Commissioner or an investigator required information or a document under section 14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person provided it within the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person had a reasonable excuse`        IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the requirement` IS AN InformationRequirement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 14(4) is committed` IF
        `the requirement`'s `the Commissioner or an investigator required information or a document under section 14(1)(b)`
    AND NOT `the requirement`'s `the person provided it within the time allowed`
    AND NOT `the requirement`'s `the person had a reasonable excuse`

`the maximum fine under section 14(4) in dollars` MEANS 10000
`the maximum imprisonment under section 14(4) in months` MEANS 6

-- s 15: obstructing, hindering or impeding the Commissioner or an investigator
-- "WITHOUT REASONABLE EXCUSE" -- a fine not exceeding $20,000 or imprisonment
-- not exceeding 12 months or both.
--
-- The HIGHEST maximum fine in the Act is for obstruction, at $20,000. Obtaining
-- a benefit dishonestly under s 11 carries $5,000. See NOTES.md.
`the maximum fine under section 15 in dollars` MEANS 20000
`the maximum imprisonment under section 15 in months` MEANS 12

GIVEN `the person obstructed, hindered or impeded the Commissioner or an investigator` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 15 is committed` IF
        `the person obstructed, hindered or impeded the Commissioner or an investigator`
    AND NOT `the person had a reasonable excuse`

§§ `16 -- Officers of bodies corporate and others`

-- s 16(1): where an offence by a BODY CORPORATE is proved (a) to have been
-- committed with the CONSENT OR CONNIVANCE of an officer, or (b) to be
-- ATTRIBUTABLE TO ANY NEGLECT on the officer's part, "the officer AS WELL AS
-- the body corporate shall be guilty".
--
-- ss 16(2) to (4) extend the same two limbs to members managing a body
-- corporate, to partners of a partnership, and to officers or governing-body
-- members of an unincorporated association. One rule, four bodies.
DECLARE BodyKind IS ONE OF
    `a body corporate`                          -- (1)
    `a body corporate managed by its members`   -- (2)
    `a partnership`                             -- (3)
    `an unincorporated association other than a partnership` -- (4)

DECLARE AttributionFacts HAS
    `the kind`                                  IS A BodyKind
    `an offence under this Act by the body is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed with the consent or connivance of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `attributable to neglect on the individual's part` IS A BOOLEAN             -- (b)

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN AttributionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is also guilty of the offence` IF
        `the facts`'s `an offence under this Act by the body is proved`
    AND `a limb of section 16 is made out` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN AttributionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a limb of section 16 is made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `committed with the consent or connivance of the individual`
    OR  `the facts`'s `attributable to neglect on the individual's part`

§§ `17 -- Composition`

-- s 17(1): the Board may compound a prescribed compoundable offence "by
-- collecting ... a sum NOT EXCEEDING THE LOWER of the following: (a) ONE HALF
-- of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence;
-- (b) $1,000."
--
-- A double ceiling, and $1,000 binds for every offence in the Act whose maximum
-- fine is above $2,000 -- which is all of them except none. The half-the-fine
-- limb can therefore never bite except on an offence with a maximum of $2,000
-- or less, and the Act creates none.
`the composition absolute ceiling in dollars` MEANS 1000

GIVEN `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the composition ceiling` IS
    IF   (0.5 TIMES `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence`)
             LESS THAN `the composition absolute ceiling in dollars`
    THEN 0.5 TIMES `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence`
    ELSE `the composition absolute ceiling in dollars`

GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` IS A NUMBER
    , `the sum collected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for that sum` IF
        `the offence is prescribed as compoundable`
    AND `the sum collected` AT MOST `the composition ceiling` `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence`

§§ `19 -- Protection from personal liability`

-- s 19(1): "NO liability is to lie personally against any of the following
-- individuals who, ACTING IN GOOD FAITH AND WITH REASONABLE CARE, does or omits
-- to do anything in the execution or purported execution of this Act" --
-- the Commissioner, Deputy and Assistant Commissioners, public officers acting
-- under the Commissioner's direction, members, officers and employees of the
-- Board, and investigators.
--
-- Two conditions, both required, and the same shape as s 19(1) of the Advance
-- Medical Directive Act: good faith is not enough without reasonable care.
DECLARE ProtectedIndividual IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner for Silver Support`                       -- (a)
    `a Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support`                  -- (b)
    `an Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support`              -- (c)
    `a public officer or employee acting under the Commissioner's direction` -- (d)
    `a member, officer or employee of the Board`                -- (e)
    `an investigator`                                           -- (f)
    `someone outside the section 19(1) list`

GIVEN `the individual` IS A ProtectedIndividual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is within the section 19(1) list` IF
    CONSIDER `the individual`
    WHEN `someone outside the section 19(1) list` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the individual` IS A ProtectedIndividual
    , `acting in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `acting with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `in the execution or purported execution of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no personal liability lies` IF
        `the individual is within the section 19(1) list` `the individual`
    AND `acting in good faith`
    AND `acting with reasonable care`
    AND `in the execution or purported execution of this Act`
